Fix "definition is marked dllimport" with GCC in qwebengineframe.h.

QWebEngineFrame::printToPdf(std::nullptr_t) is defined in the class body and
marked Q_WEBENGINECORE_EXPORT. For modules that consume QtWebEngineCore this
expands to dllimport, and GCC rejects a dllimport definition that is not
declared with the inline keyword. Every module and application that includes
the header fails to build:

  error: function 'void QWebEngineFrame::printToPdf(std::nullptr_t)'
  definition is marked dllimport

The attribute serves no purpose here: clang and GCC both ignore dllimport on
inline functions, so callers already emit their own copy. It only calls
printToPdfImpl(), which remains exported. Drop the macro.

diff --git a/src/core/api/qwebengineframe.h b/src/core/api/qwebengineframe.h
--- a/src/core/api/qwebengineframe.h
+++ b/src/core/api/qwebengineframe.h
@@ -120,7 +120,7 @@
         printToPdfImpl(QtPrivate::makeCallableObject<void(*)(std::shared_ptr<QByteArray>)>(std::move(wrappedCallback)));
     }
 #if QT_DEPRECATED_SINCE(6, 12)
-    Q_WEBENGINECORE_EXPORT void printToPdf(std::nullptr_t)
+    void printToPdf(std::nullptr_t)
     {
         printToPdfImpl(nullptr);
     }
